WEBVTT

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.690
It's morning.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.610
Oh no, I hate the daily routine.

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.270
Today's summer vacation.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.390
All right.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.570
<i>Hidamari</i>

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:03.630
<i>Make a new nameplate for the
Hidamari Apartments. Landlord</i>

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:09.710
<i>Make a new nameplate for the
Hidamari Apartments. Landlord</i>

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:11.680
<i>Make a new nameplate for the
Hidamari Apartments. Landlord</i>

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.220
<i>Make a new nameplate for the
Hidamari Apartments. Landlord</i>

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:36.940
Ano ano donna iro ga ima desuka?

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:38.210
Egao no white

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.640
Namida no blue

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.280
Kasanete mita toki

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:47.620
Honjitsu seiten nari canvas ni

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.350
Milk no ice, ramune gokun

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.020
Genki ni color topping

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:57.060
Oi. ough gaki please

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:02.960
Minna no nigaoe contest

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.730
Yuno

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:10.210
Yoshi. Ato de ''pun'' okoranai de ne

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.970
Miyako

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.470
Hiro

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:17.310
Switch osaretara wa-ha-ha

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.710
Sae

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:23.650
Nanka ii kimochi nareba ii kanji

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.190
Kyousou da

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:27.990
Ichihayaku ringo tabeyo

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:30.590
Sou ja nainda yo

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:34.260
Sou de iinda yo

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:39.200
Kudamono wa model san

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:44.040
Saa dessin shimasho ka

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.910
Shukudai dayo

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.310
<i>August 21st, Japan's Summer</i>

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:01.070
<i>We'll be making a nameplate at
Miya's place. Yuno</i>

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.700
That should do it.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:02.910
Sent

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.620
Sae, how's the sanding?

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.910
I think it's better to round
the corners a bit more.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.330
Round the corners?

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.010
You sanded too much, Miyako.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.810
Oh, it must be Hiro.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.980
Sorry to interrupt.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.020
Welcome back.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.070
Did you find some water-resistant sealer?

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.990
Your room is unexpectedly organized.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.610
Because we straightened up.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.490
There was no place to even walk a bit ago.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.870
I see.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.580
Good work.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:58.550
What made you decide to make a
nameplate here at Miya's place?

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.670
Well, that's...

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:05.010
My cheaper rent became the topic
of our conversation, and...

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.930
Cheaper? How much is it?

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:09.970
Four, zero, zero, zero, zero.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.140
Four, zero, zero... Forty-thousand yen.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:16.520
How could that be? Even the
first floor is 45,000 yen.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.980
It's the same eight tatamis wide.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:23.450
The kitchen, bath and toilet are identical.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:26.570
But only Room 202 is cheaper.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:30.120
That's a great mystery, isn't it, Chocoyama?

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.120
There goes your Stylish Detective
characterization, Lovely Chocolat.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.210
My deduction tells me that
this room might have

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:37.920
Dark Rumor

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.710
what they call a dark rumor hanging over it.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.340
A dark rumor?

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.340
Dark Rumor?

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:42.510
A dark rumor?

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:45.630
In other words, Chocoyama, it's haunted.

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:43.470
Haunted

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:49.010
H-H-Haunted. It can't be.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:56.190
I've heard that Hidamari Apartments used
to be dubbed the Bloody Apartments.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:53.430
Blood

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.610
For real?

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:03.070
There was also a time when it was
called Zip-It Apartments

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:02.070
Zi...

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:05.150
for the residents being too
noisy until midnight.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:07.450
Oh, my...

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.700
Oh, you were just joking. I got it.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.790
I was serious.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:15.960
I heard that one room in the Hidamari
Apartments was bathed in blood,

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:20.040
so, you can hear creaking even today.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:24.130
I heard it.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.130
I've never heard that before.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:31.010
Maybe your weight is causing it.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.650
How rude. I haven't even had
anything to eat today.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.440
Nothing, since the morning?

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.150
Well, I had three pieces of cake.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:55.160
What's wrong?

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.620
The floor creaked just now.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:00.960
See? When it's quiet, you can hear it.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:06.010
I usually sing when I'm alone,
so I didn't notice.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:10.050
Oh, so the faint voice I hear every
now and then is yours, Miya.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.390
You were singing until eleven
or so, weren't you?

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.230
I went to bed around nine.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:23.520
About the singing voice Yuno heard...
Who was it then?

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.570
Maybe I'm talking in my sleep.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:28.820
You talk in your sleep?

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:32.410
My parents used to say that
I sing while sleeping.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.450
So, it's more singing in your...

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:46.300
Who would have thought that we'd have a
chore like this during summer break?

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.090
Make a new nameplate for the
Hidamari Apartments. Landlord

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.090
One piece of paper made us do it.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:54.720
But isn't it nice to be able to make the
nameplate for where we live?

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.060
I think we're done with sanding.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.140
I can't wait to write letters.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:06.070
Okay, first come, first serve.
Which letter do you want to write?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.570
''Da.''

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:08.990
I like ''ma.''

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.700
Um, I'll take ''ri.''

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.070
So, I'll be doing ''hi,'' then.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:14.910
<i>Hi</i>

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:15.780
<i>Da</i>

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:16.660
<i>Ma</i>

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:17.660
<i>Ri</i>

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:20.580
It's going to be very unique.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.880
Apartments

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.880
The problem is who will write the
character for ''Apartments''?

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:27.800
Maybe we should change the name to
Chateau Hidamari or something like that,

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.720
and split ''Chateau'' into four parts?

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:34.180
Chateau Hidamari? It sounds too
fancy for these apartments.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:35.800
Well, how about Maison Hidamari?

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.140
Seven letters?

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:41.890
Golden Heights Hidamari
can be divided by four.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:43.230
Yeah, twelve letters.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:46.360
Do we have that many planks?

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:50.360
Seriously guys, we can't just
change the name, can we?

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:57.450
I wonder which color is good?

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:02.460
Why, Hiro, that's an awfully bright red.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:05.210
It's such a bold color choice for you, Hiro.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:09.090
I met Ms. Yoshinoya at school a while ago.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:13.300
Ms. Yoshinoya? It's the summer break.
Why was she at school?

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.850
Oh, Hiro.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:25.690
Ms. Yoshinoya?. What is it? You're
wearing a coat in this heat.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.400
Oh, this?

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:32.740
I've been wanting to show off
my new bathing suit.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.780
That red stuck in my mind
and I can't shake it.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.240
That must have been a real shock.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:43.160
Unbelievable, it's like a perverted old man.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:46.920
A photo e-mail just came in.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:51.550
E-mailing a photo of herself in a bathing suit...

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.550
Don't you think that the sea
is actually a picture?

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:58.760
She did that much just to send a
photo of her in a bathing suit?

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:01.220
Ms. Yoshinoya is very thorough.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:04.730
Does it mean she wanted to go to the beach?

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:07.980
The beach... Oh, I know.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.480
The beach... beach...

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:19.620
It's done. All that's left is to let it dry and coat
it with some water-resistant sealer.

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:21.700
I brought something to eat.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:26.460
Here are some icy cold herbal tea
and cooled herbal cookies.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:27.670
Yay!

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.500
They taste great.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.590
It's so refreshing and soothing.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:37.890
Did you grow these herbs in your planter?

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.470
Yes.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:41.180
Wow, you're awesome.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:45.640
Somehow I managed to pull it off,
even though I had problems like bugs.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:49.730
I'm so envious. I want to grow something.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:53.650
Like thyme, mint, lemongrass and rosemary...

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:58.200
Cabbages, carrots, onions and potatoes...

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.330
...to add to ice cream or make tea.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:04.700
...to cook curry rice or double-cooked pork.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:08.080
Also to float on the bath water.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.750
Also raise some chickens.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.540
What a gorgeous life.
What a gorgeous diet.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:15.880
Speaking of which, you were raising
something, weren't you, Yuno?

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.930
Hiro, do you mean...

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.430
Oh, no please don't.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:25.890
That was scary. It gives me goose bumps
just trying to remember it.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:30.690
I wonder what happened to her caterpillar
that transformed and flew away?

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:40.240
What's wrong?

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:44.160
Sorry, I dropped the brush,
but then it kept rolling.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.330
That's strange. I wonder if the floor is slanted?

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:50.120
Maybe it's because Hiro is sitting there.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:57.010
The flooring is coming loose.

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:01.760
Looks like this side of the floor is higher.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:02.930
Say what?

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:04.180
Wow...

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:04.640
How come you can lift it so easily?
Wow...

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:06.180
How come you can lift it so easily?

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:10.640
There are some things that look
like food dryer pouches.

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:13.110
Food dryer pouches?

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:14.360
You mean preserver bags?

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:17.940
Does this mean this apartment is defective?

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:19.900
Miyako, come with me.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:22.240
To where?

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:23.530
To the landlord's place.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:26.290
We've got to bring up this kind of issue.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:32.880
<i>Hello everyone. How's your afternoon?</i>

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:35.210
<i>Yukie ''Kani-chan'' Kanihara and...</i>

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:39.970
<i>The self-poking comedian,
Shoichi ''Yama-chan'' Yamashita present.</i>

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:41.760
We're back.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.140
Welcome back.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:44.180
Welcome.

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.890
What kind of person is the owner?

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:48.600
You haven't met?

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:53.310
No, I haven't, because my parents
did all the paperwork.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:59.110
Well, figuratively speaking,

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:03.570
I'd liken the owner to the Osaka Expo's
Tower of the Sun.

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:05.320
Tower of the Sun?

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.700
No, she's an ordinary person,
and quite a beauty too.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:11.330
Beauty? So, the owner is a woman?

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:16.170
It was worth seeing her. The mystery of
Room 202 has been solved, too.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.710
Why is the rent on Miyako's room cheaper?

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.220
Each of you can make three guesses.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.550
You have five seconds.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:27.100
Five, four, three, two...

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:27.930
Um...

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:28.680
Go ahead, Yuno.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:32.140
Maybe she put down a wrong number
at the time of signing.

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:33.230
Wrong.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.900
It's haunted, after all.

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.360
Wrong.

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:40.730
Oh, maybe it has something to do with
this loose flooring material.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.740
Yuno, you're thinking in the right direction.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:46.740
Go a bit deeper and you'll get the answer.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:51.120
The previous resident had some
kind of a large pet?

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:56.080
Given that many preserver bags,
I'd say a 'gator or something like that.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.630
It could be an iguana.

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:02.130
Maybe not a reptile, but a sea creature?

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.340
You mean like a seal or otter?

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:06.260
How did you come up with that?

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:07.180
Stop teasing and just tell us now.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.100
Sae...
Stop teasing and just tell us now.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:09.640
Stop teasing and just tell us now.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:15.270
When these apartments were remodeled,
their budget ran out.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:18.730
The owner had to remodel my room herself.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:23.320
Oh, I see, but why does it stay that way?

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:27.740
Apparently, it's because people with no
money will take the room happily.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:32.540
She wishes that people with no money
are able to pursue their goals.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:35.500
Room 202 reflects her wish.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:38.130
A nice story.

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:41.170
The owner must be really a nice person.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:44.510
Oh, but she warned us to be careful
not to dump water on the floor,

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:47.550
or those dryer bags might explode.

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:51.890
She also said that if a typhoon comes,
water might leak in.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:56.310
Considering what you two just said,
wouldn't it be really dangerous?

00:13:56.310 --> 00:14:00.810
Come to think of it, water did leak
in during the rainy season.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:03.940
<i>Hidamari Sketch</i>

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.950
It's finally done.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.160
Yeah. It looks great.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:13.910
Sae's ''hi''...

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:15.580
Miya's ''da''...

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:16.830
Hiro's ''ma''...

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:20.880
my ''ri,'' and the character, ''apartments,''
that we drew together.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.750
See? It gives off a strong impression.

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:26.550
It's not what I had imagined,
but I guess it's okay.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.850
It was fun making the nameplate.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:34.850
Today was a fulfilling day.

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:37.810
No, the real fun starts now.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:39.810
Ta-Da.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:41.900
A summer festival?

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.860
I got this at the owner's place.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:46.740
If you bring this flyer,
you can get free snacks.

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:53.200
But look, it says, only to those who
come in yukata robes.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.870
No way.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.540
Yukata? Do you have one?

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:58.830
Yeah, sort of.

00:14:58.830 --> 00:14:59.830
Miya...

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:03.290
Checkered pattern... I can make a modern one.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:04.590
The curtain?

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:06.340
Are you going to make one now?

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:11.300
Yukata. I'll become an icon of the
summer and get my snacks.

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:13.180
Miya, calm down.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:17.220
Oh, I know. I have one I used to wear.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:19.640
Let's see...

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:20.810
Oh, here.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.520
I can't wait.

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:23.940
What kind of pattern is it?

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:26.730
Magical Girl Minky...

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:28.490
A character pattern?

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:32.240
Okay, it's done.

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:33.910
Miya, does it fit?

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.240
How's the size?

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:38.200
It's pretty good. It's a perfect fit.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.330
It looks pretty cute.

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:47.250
It looks rather fashionable.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:50.050
Am I the only one who thinks
she looks like a hooker?

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:52.840
Sorry that we kept you waiting.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:56.140
It took a while to put this on. My apologies.

00:15:56.140 --> 00:16:00.100
At first, Sae put it on like a guy.

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:01.770
Do you need a date?

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:03.400
No, I don't.

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:09.610
I can hear the festival music.

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:11.030
It's already begun.

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:16.240
I like festival music. It makes me excited.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:18.330
Do you want to use it as a ring tone?

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.290
It might be good for your alarm clock.

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:23.250
I think it would be perfect for
railroad crossings too.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:25.130
Railroad crossings?

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:36.800
Bouncing Ball

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:36.800
Roasted Corn

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:41.680
Woo-hoo. Festival, here I come.

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:43.770
Hey, Miya, wait.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:48.900
Hiro, that yukata is very clean.
You've had it since you were little, right?

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:51.360
I only wore it twice.

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:53.400
Only twice?

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:57.450
Yes, that yukata is jinxed.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:58.660
Jinxed?

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.910
The first time I wore it,

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:04.080
there was no octopus in the takoyaki
dumplings I bought at a kiosk,

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.170
all eight of them in the box.

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:08.670
That's unfortunate.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:12.510
And the second time,
one of the booths collapsed on me.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:14.220
Ouch...

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.380
Hi, everyone, good evening.

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:18.930
Ms. Yoshinoya?.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:20.890
She's wearing a normal yukata.

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:26.730
Of course, there's no way she'd
wear a bikini to a festival.

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:28.230
Anything wrong?

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:29.310
Nothing.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:32.610
Ms. Yoshinoya, your yukata is pretty.

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:34.570
A rose pattern?

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:41.410
You all look great in yukata,
especially Miyako's is very cute.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:45.790
I'll use it as an inspiration for my costume.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.500
Well, see you later.

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:52.170
The seventh one.

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.340
Wow.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.720
Miya, you're great at catching
water balloon yo-yos.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:00.930
I was very poor when I was little.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:04.220
My allowance at the festival was only
enough to pay for one game.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:05.270
Wow...

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:08.270
So, I traded the yo-yos that I got in one game
for all kinds of stuff my friends had.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.690
Amazing.
So, I traded the yo-yos that I got in one game
for all kinds of stuff my friends had.

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:12.520
Like three yo-yos for one takoyaki dumpling.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:16.950
I just love festivals.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:18.700
Yeah, it's fun.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.370
I managed to get a bag of snacks, too.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.660
Wow, it comes with some fireworks.

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:28.500
This is a mouse tail firework. I love this.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:31.540
I'm the opposite.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:38.380
It always chases me, so I had to have
my cat with me when I was little.

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:40.430
How cute.

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:45.850
Wow, it's pretty.

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:49.100
But it's tiny, isn't it?

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:52.190
Yeah, we wanted to see big fireworks too.

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:59.490
Miya, you're so mean.

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:04.990
Hey, Hiro, why did you keep
the jinxed yukata?

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:10.460
Oh, that's because a divine fox spirit
is attached to the yukata.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:12.500
A divine fox?

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:15.840
If bad things happen, the same number
of good things will happen too.

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:19.760
So, I should keep it.
That's what my grandmother told me.

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:21.970
A divine fox?

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:26.850
I wonder if it attracts bad
luck when you wear it?

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:29.060
But you are making Miyako wear it.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:33.650
But if it was Yuno, it'd look too perfect.

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:35.860
That's not what I meant.

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:41.400
What's wrong, Miya?

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:47.700
I can hear the booming sound of fireworks.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.330
Eh? You mean the big ones?

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:54.250
Wait up, Miya, I don't hear anything.

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:25.700
What Miya said turned out to be true.

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:32.870
Wow, that's beautiful.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:37.040
That's awesome, Tamaya.

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:39.550
Aloha.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:40.800
That should be Kagiya.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:48.220
That was fun.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:53.270
I wonder why only Miya heard
the sound of fireworks?

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:57.690
Do you think it's because of the yukata?

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:02.190
Maybe, but if so, a divine fox
is definitely with her.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.110
I want to eat some inari.

00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:09.080
<i>The Hundred Famous Japanese Spas Series</i>

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:13.500
The summer festival was fun.

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:17.880
Only Miya heard the sound
of fireworks before us.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:22.880
Hiro said it could be because the yukata
is possessed by a fox spirit.

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.630
What happened, Miya?

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:30.050
Yunocchi, weren't you eating
a snow cone just now?

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:33.180
I'm taking a bath.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:38.610
Strange, I heard the sound of
someone shaving ice.

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:41.480
I didn't hear anything like that.

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:45.450
If this isn't the right place, it must be Hiro.

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:52.160
My snow cone? How did you know, Miya?

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:55.960
Maybe she just happens to
have incredible hearing?

00:21:56.370 --> 00:22:01.920
But Miya looked like she was possessed
by something earlier.

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:08.890
<i>The end of August 21st
To Be Continued</i>

